{"agent":"impl-tool-diet","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_families` computes `single=f in HOT_SINGLES`, but `resolve` accepts a declared `Command` whose `family` is a hot-single name with a non-empty `action`. The generated `Family` is then marked `single=True` even though its `members` map contains both the hot single’s empty action and the extra action. For example, with `ddflow_identify` in `TOOLS` and a command `ddflow_extra` declared as `family=\"ddflow_identify\", action=\"extra\"`, `_families` returns `Family(\"ddflow_identify\", {\"\": \"ddflow_identify\", \"extra\": \"ddflow_extra\"}, single=True)`. A caller that sees `single=True` omits the action enum, making `extra` unreachable and breaking the hot-single invariant, while no error is raised.","digest":"f01a95076bb1da28","location":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/families.py:135","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/families.py:135"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The test passes `legacy={}`, so it never introduces a conflicting legacy mapping. A `resolve` implementation that prioritizes legacy entries whenever present would still pass this test because no legacy entry exists. The input `legacy={\"ddflow_zed_go\": (\"ddflow_legacy\", \"old\")}` is what would actually distinguish “declared wins” from “legacy wins”, and it is absent.","digest":"54978886265d8084","location":"tests/test_declared_families.py:test_a_declared_family_and_action_win_over_the_legacy_placement","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_declared_families.py:test_a_declared_family_and_action_win_over_the_legacy_placement"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`fam.members` is a dict, so `len(set(fam.members)) == len(fam.members)` is tautologically true: dict keys are unique by construction, and duplicate action keys would already have been collapsed by assignment. For example, a generated members dict that assigns `\"record\"` twice silently overwrites the first value, and this test still sees one key and passes, so it cannot catch duplicate action generation.","digest":"a089eb9bebc79861","location":"tests/test_declared_families.py:test_actions_are_unique_within_a_family","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_declared_families.py:test_actions_are_unique_within_a_family"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The test checks `F.HOT_SINGLES` against a separate hardcoded tuple and then checks counts, but it never verifies that the families with `single=True` are exactly `F.HOT_SINGLES`. Swapping the `single=True` flag between `ddflow_gate` and `ddflow_brief` keeps `len(fams) == 15`, `len(F.FAMILIES) == 24`, and the `F.HOT_SINGLES` tuple comparison passing, so the property named in the test is not actually asserted.","digest":"28c8f549eb357273","location":"tests/test_declared_families.py:test_nine_hot_singles_and_fifteen_families_make_24_tools","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_declared_families.py:test_nine_hot_singles_and_fifteen_families_make_24_tools"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":10130,"diff_sha":"e70641dc2e5fab0cd7661a9ee43ef2a964a5b9165674f13a44018fd9ed78e4f2","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":719.1,"family":"deepseek","findings":4,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"5ff7404e500adb14","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/MTD-family-spec.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261022T135807Z-9460849e.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"04f92df0c4c87eefde02673546f787d9beeaedba","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/surfaces/registry.py":"100644 9b4cc99d204a98378d14772420c47386c4be3386","ddflow/surfaces/tools/families.py":"100644 28d38252d215166750c61ed333e5603708abf970","tests/test_declared_families.py":"100644 62b6e3c3d3f9da9757aa702b07350138574181da"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1